# Overview
PROJECT IDENTITY
- This project is a Flutter-based dynamic mobile app generator.
- It is NOT a traditional Flutter application.

CORE MODEL
- Applications, screens, components, and themes are defined as data.
- Flutter is used only as a runtime rendering platform.
- UI structure must never be hardcoded in Dart.

ARCHITECTURAL LAYERS
- Config Layer:
  - Pure declarative data
  - No logic, no Flutter, no rendering
  - Single source of truth for app definition

- Engine Layer:
  - Interprets configuration into UI
  - Resolves templates and component mappings
  - Owns rendering orchestration
  - Contains no business logic

- Core Layer:
  - Stateless, reusable UI primitives
  - Configuration-agnostic
  - No JSON parsing or template logic

- Features Layer:
  - Isolated business domains
  - Independent from the Engine
  - Must not affect UI generation logic

STRICT CONSTRAINTS
- Do NOT hardcode screens, flows, or layouts.
- Do NOT embed business or domain logic in widgets or renderers.
- Do NOT couple UI decisions to Flutter-specific constructs.
- Do NOT treat this system as a template-based app.

DESIGN INTENT
- Any visual or structural change must be achievable via configuration.
- Code changes are allowed only for engine capabilities or shared primitives.

VIOLATIONS
- Any solution that mixes UI rendering with business logic is invalid.
- Any per-merchant branching or duplicated UI code is rejected.
